    "title": "Spinach downy mildew risk HIGH – Pachi Coast",
    "body": "Leaves estimated wet 13-15 h every night since the rain of Thu 12-Fri 13 Nov, nights 6.0-9.0 °C, and the front on Fri 20-Sun 22 Nov brings 27.5 mm. Pachi had downy mildew in Dec 2025. This spinach is 67% grown, harvest from Thu 3 Dec – there is time for one protective spray that clears its PHI before harvest.",
    "action": "See recommendation R01: one protective spray Wed 18 Nov (mandipropamid, FRAC 40). Before spraying, check lower-leaf undersides for grey-violet fuzzy growth (sporulation); yellow patches alone are not proof.",
    "why_rule": "High when leaf wetness >= 10 h on >= 3 of the last 5 nights with night temp 5-15 °C, AND rain forecast within 5 days, AND parcel has mildew history.",
